The pyfix test data is taken from a couple of different sources:

  - rest.ica.zip contains a MELODIC analysis performed on the "nice" data set
    from the FSL Course FMRI 3 practical
  - Atlas.dtseries.nii is some hand-created CIfTI time series data with the
    same number of time points as the fMRI data in rest.ica.zip. The data
    in this file is from the raw fMRI data from voxels (53, 11, 27), (48, 7, 42),
    (31, 17, 42), (33, 12, 27), (30, 78, 43), (30, 12, 32), and (32, 4, 29).
  - rest.ica.fixdir.zip contains the fix/ directory from running the original
    (MATLAB/R) version of FIX on rest.ica.zip
  - training_data.zip contains features.csv and hand_labels_noise.txt files,
    for 100 subjects, from the publicly available "Standard" FIX training data
    set (https://www.fmrib.ox.ac.uk/datasets/FIX-training/).
  - training.pyfix_model is a pyfix model trained on training_data.zip.
  - cleaned_data.zip contains the results of running the original FIX on
    rest.ica.zip, with a few different variants of "fix -a". A ROI of the
    cleaned 4D data is stored to save space - the ROI parameters are stored in
    fslroi_params.txt.
  - training.RData is an original FIX model trained on the first five subjects
    from the "Standard" FIX training data set.
